## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design concrete, layered security controls for a common integration risk in SaaS platforms. It tests understanding of both transport-layer and application-layer protections.

## Key Concepts
- Webhook signature verification using HMAC
- Replay protection via timestamps and narrow validation windows
- Secret management and rotation policies
- Transport security with mutual TLS (mTLS)

## Code Example
```javascript
const crypto = require('crypto');

function verifyWebhookSignature(payload, secret, signature, timestamp, windowMs = 300000) {
  const now = Date.now();
  if (now - timestamp > windowMs) return false;
  const data = \`${timestamp}.${payload}\`;
  const expected = crypto.createHmac('sha256', secret).update(data).digest('hex');
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(signature), Buffer.from(expected));
}
```
